       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day for inpatient anti-inflammatory dosing. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high carries a significant risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **400 mg four times daily**, for 1,600 mg/day\n- **800 mg three times daily**, for 2,400 mg/day\n- **800 mg four times daily**, for 3,200 mg/day, which is the maximum\n- **1600 mg per day in total**, split into a different schedule\n- **Another dose**\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I can then enter it with a note recording that it is an intentional above-maximum dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
